WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.390
2018's superhero body count was impressive
to say the least, but 2019's promises to stack

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:11.320
at least as high - mostly thanks to the many
landmark movies, shows and comic storylines

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.900
that have been released over the course of
the year.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.720
Obviously, there are spoilers ahead, and before
you ask about the MCU's Black Widow and Iron

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.140
Man, just remember that earlier this year
we covered superheroes who sadly died in the

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.380
first half of 2019, so if you want to see
them make sure you check out our previous

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:27.880
video!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.240
After the whole Thanos thing that's been going
down in the MCU these last couple of years,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.200
Marvel might be forgiven for thinking they
had the edge on killing off characters by

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.820
scrubbing them from existence.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:45.100
But CW's The Flash begs to differ, since that's
how the speedster XS - also known as Nora

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.420
West-Allen - was killed off in the show's
season 5 finale.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:55.700
During this episode, XS gets erased from reality
when Team Flash's defeat of the villain Cicada

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.340
changes Nora's future timeline.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:03.120
In an earlier episode, the show's heroes learn
Nora has been running to and from the future,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.060
getting tips on how to beat Cicada from the
imprisoned villain, Reverse-Flash.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.860
But in the finale, the team figures out Reverse-Flash's
motivation - in the future, Cicada's dagger

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.320
keeps Reverse-Flash powerless, so he wants
Flash to destroy it.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:22.800
Regardless of this discovery, the team is
forced to destroy Cicada's dagger.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.080
Hoping to tie up loose ends, they then travel
to the future to stop Reverse-Flash.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.499
The heroes seem to be winning the fight, but
Nora begins suffering the effects of the timeline

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.000
change.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.640
Reverse-Flash tells the heroes the only way
to save Nora is for her to enter his "Negative

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.659
Speed Force," but she refuses - not wanting
to suffer from the negative emotions necessary

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:44.460
to access it.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.580
Reverse-Flash escapes and Nora dies embracing
her mother and father.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.360
You'd be on shaky ground calling Raven's comic
book counterpart - the Marvel version, not

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:00.209
the Teen Titan - a superhero, since she tends
to just veer between moral ambiguity and outright

00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:00.800
villainy.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.060
But ever since 2011's X-Men: First Class,
the movie franchise's Raven, also known as

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:11.970
Mystique, has been one of the good guys - and
she pays dearly for her heroics in 2019's

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:12.960
Dark Phoenix.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.120
Shortly after Jean Grey leaves the mansion,
it becomes clear that Professor X not only

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.760
psychically blocked Jean's traumatic childhood
memories, but lied to her about the fate of

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.260
her father.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.780
Because of this, Charles knows where to look
for Jean after she leaves - her father's home.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.780
Once they find her, the X-Men are no match
for the emerging Phoenix.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.459
She easily fights them off, even injuring
Quicksilver so badly he's benched for the

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.360
rest of the film.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:44.510
When Raven tries to talk Jean down, an out-of-control
Jean flings Raven back through the air.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.160
The blue-skinned mutant is impaled on a piece
of wreckage.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.740
"I love you."

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.900
Raven's death brings with it catastrophic
consequences.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:03.280
Magneto emerges to seek revenge on Phoenix,
Beast leaves the X-Men to help Magneto, and

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.120
the X-Men and Magneto's followers find themselves
on an all-too-familiar collision course.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:14.519
Better known as the Hellfire Club's Black
Queen, the comic book version of Selene Gallio

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:21.080
doesn't even enjoy the occasional act of moral
ambiguity Mystique does - she's 100% bad guy.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:26.640
But just like her actual abilities, the morality
of Dark Phoenix's Selene is vastly different

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:27.800
from the comic version.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:33.290
The film first depicts Selene as one of the
inhabitants of the island Genosha, where Magneto

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.320
oversees a growing community of mutant refugees.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.430
Along with Beast and Ariki, Magneto brings
Selene with him to New York City to kill Phoenix,

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.880
and she spends most of that fight using her
own telepathic abilities to keep Professor

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:47.920
X's powers busy.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.160
After all the mutants are captured by a government
strike force and loaded onto a train, Selene

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.220
joins the X-Men against a horde of invading
aliens.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.040
Unfortunately, Selene doesn't survive the
battle.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.020
During a lull in the fight against the aliens…well,
this happens.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.740
And sure, her body is never actually shown,
but since this version of the character isn't

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:14.320
nearly as powerful as her comic counterpart,
her fate is nonetheless clear enough.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:20.079
As far as anyone knows, Melissa Benoist will
continue playing Supergirl well into the future,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.860
but season 4 of Supergirl saw one of her characters
killed off nonetheless.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.140
This season had Benoist doing double duty
as both Supergirl and a clone raised in the

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.180
fictional Eastern European nation of Kaznia.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:38.220
The clone was initially referred to as Snowbird
and later nicknamed Red Daughter, referring

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:44.360
to the classic DC Elseworlds miniseries Superman:
Red Son, which had Kal-El raised in the Soviet

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.000
Union rather than Kansas.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:51.860
Lex Luthor allies himself with the Kaznians
and uses the opportunity to manipulate Red

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:52.820
Daughter and win her loyalty.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:58.710
Unfortunately, in Supergirl's season 4 finale,
Red Daughter learns Lex's loyalty only goes

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.320
one way.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:04.780
Lex fools the Kaznians into believing he's
supporting an invasion of the United States,

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.930
when in fact he uses the opportunity to destroy
the invading Kaznians and falsely prove himself

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.420
as a hero to the U.S.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.500
When Supergirl confronts Luthor with what
he's done, she finds herself needing Red Daughter's

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.000
help.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:22.320
The clone eventually dies coming between Lex
and Supergirl, after Lex tries to blast the

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.260
show's hero with Kryptonite energy.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.540
The Kryptonite kills Red Daughter, but as
she dies she releases a wave of energy - which

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.400
Supergirl uses to grow strong enough to finally
defeat Luthor.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:38.400
The second episode of Amazon Prime's The Boys
sees the series claim its first superhero

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.320
victim, but it's far from the last.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.760
Translucent is captured by the Boys after
he follows Hughie from the Seven's headquarters

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.040
and attacks him at his electronics store job.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:53.240
Hughie and Billy Butcher manage to incapacitate
Translucent, but can't kill him because of

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.600
his super-dense skin.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:59.860
Butcher then brings the unconscious hero to
his old colleague Frenchie, who eventually

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:03.780
has the idea to insert a bomb into the incapacated
hero.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.840
With Hughie still new to life as an outlaw,
the notion of gruesomely killing Translucent

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.780
doesn't sit well with him.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.440
And sure enough, towards the end of the second
episode, he waits until he's alone with the

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.729
hero and proceeds to free him from his cage.

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:21.410
But before Translucent can escape, Hughie
changes his mind and sets off the bomb inside

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.560
the supe, blowing him to smithereens.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:28.300
The comic book The Boys is based on tends
to be much bloodier than the show, though

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:33.940
in this case the series handled Hughie's "christening"
into Butcher's world in a much darker fashion.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.020
Like the show, Hughie is the first member
of the Boys to kill a supe in the comic - he

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:41.440
kills the young Blarney from the team Teenage
Kix.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:45.960
But Blarney's death at Hughie's hands in the
comic is an accident, while the Hughie of

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.100
the show knows exactly what he's doing when
he kills Translucent.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:54.440
The accidental death of Hughie's girlfriend
Robin by the speedster hero A-Train is what

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.460
sends Hughie on his quest for justice.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:01.800
Before his death, Translucent reveals that
A-Train was with his girlfriend Popclaw before

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.660
he killed Robin.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.940
The Boys would likely have never discovered
this on their own, as A-Train has been keeping

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:11.610
his relationship with Popclaw a secret because
she's seen as being something of a C-Lister

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.980
in the superhero community.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:16.280
This news makes Popclaw a perfect target for
the Boys.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:21.050
Posing as workmen, they plant surveillance
devices in her apartment, and when Popclaw

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:25.360
accidentally kills her landlord, the Boys
are there to blackmail her into giving them

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:25.960
information.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:31.979
When A-Train later finds out that word has
got out about the drug Compound-V, he forces

00:07:31.979 --> 00:07:36.180
Popclaw to go into hiding, worried that Homelander
might find out about her.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:41.080
At the same time, A-Train correctly suspects
Popclaw might be the Boys' source for their

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:41.640
information.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.280
When she finally admits what happened with
her landlord and the Boys, A-Train uses his

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:50.979
super speed to grab two syringes of heroin
and injects them into Popclaw before she can

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:51.480
stop him.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.000
She then dies from the ensuing overdose.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.819
The most brutal death in the first season
of The Boys is surely that of Mesmer, a mind-reading

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:04.180
former teen hero who has since fallen into
obscurity and been relegated to the convention

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:04.680
circuit.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.380
"So what am I thinking of…"

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.260
"We're thinking of the same thing."

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:12.180
"Cool."

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.100
In episode 6, Frenchie and Mother's Milk track
down Mesmer at a convention and convince him

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:18.660
to help them.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:23.780
In return, Mother's Milk promises to reunite
Mesmer with the daughter he hasn't seen in

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:24.280
years.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:29.140
Butcher isn't happy when he finds out Frenchie
and Mother's Milk have gone to a supe for

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.300
help, however, and unfortunately his fears
come true.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.000
By the end of the sixth episode, Mesmer has
given Homelander information on every last

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:41.680
one of the Boys, in the hopes it will win
him favor with the Seven and bring him back

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.020
to the inner circle of successful superheroes.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:49.260
Homelander takes Mesmer's phone, which contains
photographs of the Boys, and flies off.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.560
Of course, Mesmer's reward never materializes...at
least, not the one he was hoping for.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.100
Butcher catches the psychic as he tries to
flee the city and beats him to death in a

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:04.210
public restroom - but not before he tells
Mesmer to use his powers on him, so the supe

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.340
can see exactly what Butcher's planning to
do to him.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:12.000
If you've been following Titans' second season,
then you know something has been brewing with

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:15.380
the team regarding a past conflict with the
mercenary Deathstroke.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:21.060
In the second season's fourth episode, things
finally kick off after Garth, also known as

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.540
Aqualad, is killed off.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:28.070
Aqualad spends most of the episode trying
to woo Donna Troy, and it's clear he's had

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.400
a thing for her for years.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:34.000
They finally sleep together toward the end
of the episode, but it's only hours before

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.400
Donna Troy plans to secretly leave Titans
Tower for Themyscira.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.920
Once Dick Grayson tells Aqualad what Donna's
planning, Aqualad finds Donna at the airport

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.640
to profess his love and, he hopes, stop her
from leaving.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.870
He catches Donna and her older mentor Jillian
before they get on the plane, and things look

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:58.000
hopeful for their young love...before Deathstroke
fires on them from a hidden position.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:03.020
Garth turns and protects Donna from the bullet,
taking it in the chest and dying.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:07.660
Donna and Jillian manage to escape, and by
the end of the episode Donna and the rest

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.600
of the Titans are ready to exact their vengeance.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:16.380
The line-wide Marvel Comics story War of the
Realms was one of Marvel's biggest events

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.380
in 2019.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:23.240
And in War of the Realms #2, Asgard loses
one of its favorite daughters - Valkyrie.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:29.760
Fighting atop a pile of slain trolls and dark
elves, Valkyrie reaches out to Malekith, architect

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.860
of the War of the Realms, to stop hiding and
face her.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:38.460
Malekith surprises her and stabs her from
behind, and the issue ends with the dark elf

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:39.960
mercilessly beheading her.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:45.940
While this seems a conclusive end to a character
as you'll find in any Marvel comic, Malekith

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.200
doesn't rid the world of Valkyrie, though
he does kill Brunnhilde.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:56.450
Three weeks before the release of War of the
Realms #2, Marvel's Editor-in-Chief CB Cebulski

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:01.829
announced at Chicago's C2E2 convention that
a new Valkyrie comic would spin out of War

00:11:01.829 --> 00:11:02.620
of the Realms.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:07.220
The day after issue two's release, news broke
that it would not be Brunnhilde's spirit would

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.520
pass the mantle of Valkyrie to Jane Foster.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:14.410
Foster is played by Natalie Portman in the
MCU films, and in the comics took over the

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:20.760
mantle of Thor for four years, until being
forced to sacrifice Mjolnir to stop the monstrous

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.000
Mangog in 2018's Mighty Thor #705.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:30.560
Last year, the MCU's Heimdall died at Thanos'
hands in the opening scene of Avengers: Infinity

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:31.080
War.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:37.079
In Valkyrie: Jane Foster #2, Heimdall's comic
book counterpart dies as well, though the

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.920
villain who kills him isn't quite as powerful
as Thanos.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:44.640
War of the Realms had come to an end by this
point, but the shockwaves are still being

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.960
felt across the universe.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:51.120
Jane Foster replaced the late Brunnhilde as
Valkyrie at the end of the event, launching

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.320
her new solo series Valkyrie: Jane Foster.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:58.880
In the first issue, Foster defeats some minor
villains who stole the original Valkyrie's

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.700
sword after her death, but one of them gets
away.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:07.020
The sword, Dragonfang, is claimed by the psychotic
Daredevil villain Bullseye.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.400
As the issue ends, Bullseye runs Heimdall
through with Dragonfang from behind.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:17.540
Heimdall initially survives and helps Foster
battle the villain, but later dies from his

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.220
wounds after successfully destroying Dragonfang.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.399
As he dies, he begs Foster not to take him
to Valhalla, but to bring him beyond the ten

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.200
realms so he can see what is there.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:34.220
Foster agrees, promising to embark on a "Journey
Into Mystery" with the late bridge-keeper,

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:38.680
echoing the title of the comic in which Marvel's
Thor first appeared in 1962.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:45.380
Tony Stark: Iron Man #15 sees the return of
an old friend to the Marvel universe: an artificial

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.430
intelligence version of Tony Stark.

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.360
"Oh, it's good to be back."

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:56.820
The Stark A.I. became active after the events
Civil War II left Tony in a coma.

00:12:56.829 --> 00:13:02.560
It acted as a mentor to Riri WIlliams, also
known as Ironheart, and occupied one of Tony's

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:06.800
suits to help his friends against Hydra in
the Marvel-wide Secret Empire event.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:12.450
The real Stark, now out of his coma, testifies
in front of Congress in Tony Stark: Iron Man

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:17.260
#15, and one of the senators has somehow gotten
his hands on the Stark A.I.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:22.380
He reactivates it in the middle of the proceedings,
and when Iron Man is attacked by a bizarre

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:27.440
android comprised of the fused bodies of Vision
and Wonder Man, the A.I. is there to help

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:27.940
him.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:34.480
Unfortunately, Tony knows the only thing that
will stop the android is an EMP cascade, which

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.920
will also kill off the A.I.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:41.300
The Stark A.I. tells him to go through with
it anyway, sacrificing itself in the process.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.420
But that's not all.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.680
Since the beginning of Tony Stark: Iron Man,
Tony and his colleagues have been dealing

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:51.320
with the notion of whether or not artificial
intelligence deserve the same rights as humans.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:57.800
While Stark is testifying, there are A.I.-driven
robots out protesting in the street...and

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.620
his EMP cascade kills off all of them as well.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:05.810
With the deaths of Kid Loki and Valkyrie,
the Asgardians of the Galaxy arguably suffer

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:10.600
more than any other superhero team in Marvel's
War of the Realms event.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:16.760
Asgardians of the Galaxy #10, the series finale,
takes one more victim from the Asgardians'

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:21.800
ranks, as Skurge the Executioner makes a last
stand that is brimming with dark irony.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:27.339
Skurge was freshly resurrected when he joined
the Asgardians of the Galaxy, as his previous

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:30.260
death was one of the most memorable in Marvel
Comics history.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:37.680
He died in the 1985 classic Thor #362, fighting
off waves of undead soldiers to give his Asgardian

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.600
brethren time to escape Hel.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:42.220
"For Asgard…"

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.740
This time around, however, Skurge's foes are
much different.

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:58.610
The angels of Heven inexplicably side with
the Dark Elf Malekith in War of the Realms,

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:02.940
and Skurge ends up joining fellow Asgardian
Angela in Heven itself.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:08.360
Once there, Skurge holds off the angels to
give Angela the time to summon an army of

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.040
undead Asgardian warriors.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:15.730
Ironically, having died his first death against
an army of the dead, Skurge dies his second

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:19.340
death helping to summon another army of the
dead to his side.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:25.040
After he succumbs to his wounds and the battle
is won, Skurge awakes in Valhalla, the realm

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.040
of the honored dead.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:31.190
Valhalla's other residents greet him warmly,
and when he insists he hasn't earned a place

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:35.080
among them, they tell him they all thought
the same thing when they got there.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:40.700
Dark Beast is a version of Hank McCoy from
an alternate reality based on the 1995 Age

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.720
of Apocalypse event - and, to be fair, he
wasn't much of a superhero.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:49.660
Nevertheless, he's been working with the X-Men
since Cyclops returned from the dead and started

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.880
putting a new team together in Uncanny X-Men
#11.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:58.860
In Uncanny X-Men #20, Dark Beast inadvertently
turns on his benefactors, thinking he's helping

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.180
them, but pays for his mistake with his life.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:06.560
All around the globe, parents are giving their
children a new vaccine designed to suppress

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.300
any emerging mutant genes.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:13.140
Dark Beast tells his teammates he's figured
out a way to counteract the vaccine.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:16.260
He just needs his own agent dispersed in the
upper atmosphere.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:22.180
Unfortunately, the X-Men trust Dark Beast,
and Banshee disperses the agent as ordered.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:27.819
The X-Men soon learn what Dark Beast failed
to tell them: that, once his agent has been

00:16:27.819 --> 00:16:32.970
dispersed, it wouldn't simply stop the anti-mutant
vaccine from working; if a child receiving

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.360
the vaccine is a mutant, it will likely kill
them.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:43.120
Dark Beast sees this as an inestimable success,
saying that now human parents won't dare get

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.360
their children vaccinated.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:51.459
Ignoring Cyclops' protests, the vengeful mutant
Magik uses her powers to teleport Dark Beast's

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.100
head into the ceiling, ending his dark experiments
for good.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:01.300
The current volume of Guardians of the Galaxy
spun out of the line-wide event Infinity Wars

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.660
in which Gamora kills her adoptive father
Thanos.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:10.280
In Guardians of the Galaxy #1 it is revealed
that Thanos had arranged to have his consciousness

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:14.240
uploaded into someone else's body in case
of his untimely death.

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:21.180
Starfox then assembles a team of "Dark Guardians"
to find and kill the most likely candidates,

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:24.660
starting with Gamora - while Peter Quill's
Guardians try to save her.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:30.280
Unfortunately for Starfox and his Dark Guardians,
it turns out Gamora isn't the new host for

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.320
Thanos after all.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:37.840
In Guardians of the Galaxy #5, it's revealed
that it was Starfox into whom Thanos' consciousness

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:42.720
was uploaded, and it was the Asgardian goddess
of death, Hela, who did the deed.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:48.140
After the Dark Guardians capture Gamora, Hela
appears and easily brushes them aside.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:53.440
She reveals the truth to Starfox and Thanos'
consciousness emerges and gains dominance

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:54.800
over his brother's body.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.660
Hela then brings Starfox to Knowhere, where
Thanos' reassembled body awaits.

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:04.680
The Guardians arrive on Knowhere, and Gamora
runs Starfox through - ending his life and

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.580
stopping the Mad Titan's resurrection.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:13.540
The long-awaited CW crossover "Crisis on Infinite
Earths" finally arrived as 2019 approached

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:18.120
its end, and the event's first chapter wasted
no time in taking a major victim.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.160
Oliver Queen, a.k.a. Green Arrow.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:27.710
He sacrifices himself in the first episode
to save the population of the besieged Earth-38,

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:29.640
home of the Arrowverse's Supergirl.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:35.270
As anti-matter waves threaten to destroy all
the universes in the multiverse, heroes from

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:41.480
most of the CW's superhero series are summoned
by the Monitor to save Earth-38 and evacuate

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.920
over 3 billion of its people to Earth-1.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:49.430
As the heroes fight off the Anti-Monitor's
armies, the Monitor determines Earth-38 is

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.820
lost and transports the heroes away.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:54.420
Green Arrow, however, refuses to leave.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:57.620
The Monitor finally brings Oliver back to
Earth-1.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:02.740
"I calculate 1 billion souls survived due
to his noble sacrifice."

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.380
Oliver dies shortly afterward.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:10.100
But he does get resurrected, sort of, in part
3, he's brought back without a soul.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:15.260
After a group of heroes goes to Purgatory
to save him, Jim Corrigan, The Spectre in

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:18.400
the comics, tells him that he's needed elsewhere
to fulfill his destiny.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:24.910
By Part Three of "Crisis on Infinite Earths,"
all the heroes of the multiverse are dead.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:32.100
The only survivors are Supergirl, Batwoman,
Ryan Choi, Lex Luthor, Flash, J'onn J'onzz,

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.160
and Sara Lance.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:40.530
Titans' Hawk and Robin of Earth-9, the 1960s
Batman series' Earth-66 Robin, and Birds of

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:46.530
Prey's Earth-203 Huntress, and everyone from
their respective worlds, are all annihilated

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:52.790
by the anti-matter wave, Batwoman kills the
Earth-99 Batman, and Lex Luthor kills and

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.300
replaces the Earth-96 Superman.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:20:01.980
Earth-90 Flash sacrifices himself to save
Earth-1, which unfortunately proves futile

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.000
after the Harbinger kills The Monitor.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:10.120
The long list of other dead heroes include
everyone on Earth-2, Earth-89 Batman and any

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:16.580
members of his Bat family, the Ray and Freedom
Fighters of Earth-X, the Mick Rory of Earth-74,

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:23.330
the heroes of Earth-38, the former Superman
and other heroes of Earth-167, Black Lightning,

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.240
Thunder, Lightning, Pariah, and Jonah Hex.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:30.420
Those aren't all the superheroes who lost
their lives in 2019.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:33.260
Here are a few other heroes who fell this
year.

